sequenceDiagram
    autonumber

    participant User as User / Data Scientist
    participant Dashboard as ODH Dashboard<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS
    participant Controller as Notebook Controller<br/>Watch mTLS
    participant Registry as Container Registry<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant KRBP as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP TLS
    participant JupyterLab as JupyterLab<br/>8888/TCP HTTP
    participant DSPA as DSPA Endpoint<br/>443/TCP HTTPS
    participant S3 as S3 Object Storage<br/>443/TCP HTTPS

    rect rgb(232, 244, 253)
        Note over User,JupyterLab: Flow 1: Workbench Pod Startup
        User->>Dashboard: Select workbench image<br/>HTTPS / OpenShift OAuth
        Dashboard->>K8sAPI: Create Notebook CR<br/>HTTPS / Service Account
        K8sAPI->>Controller: Watch event<br/>mTLS / Service Account
        Controller->>Registry: Pull workbench image<br/>HTTPS / Image pull secret
        Controller->>Controller: Inject kube-rbac-proxy sidecar,<br/>CA bundles, DSPA secret
        Note over Controller: Creates Pod with<br/>workbench container +<br/>kube-rbac-proxy sidecar
        User->>KRBP: Access workbench<br/>HTTPS / Bearer Token
        KRBP->>JupyterLab: Forward request<br/>HTTP (pod-internal, no auth)
        JupyterLab-->>KRBP: JupyterLab UI
        KRBP-->>User: HTTPS response
    end

    rect rgb(225, 190, 231)
        Note over User,S3: Flow 2: Elyra Pipeline Execution
        participant RuntimePod as Runtime Pod<br/>(Pipeline Image)
        User->>DSPA: Submit pipeline via Elyra UI<br/>HTTPS / Bearer Token
        DSPA->>Registry: Pull runtime image<br/>HTTPS / Image pull secret
        Note over DSPA,RuntimePod: Creates pipeline pod with<br/>runtime image
        RuntimePod->>S3: Read/write data artifacts<br/>HTTPS / Access Key or IAM
        RuntimePod->>RuntimePod: Execute bootstrapper.py<br/>(pipeline node logic)
        RuntimePod-->>DSPA: Pipeline step complete
    end

    rect rgb(255, 243, 224)
        Note over Controller,JupyterLab: Flow 3: Code-Server Activity Tracking (Idle Culling)
        participant Nginx as nginx<br/>80/TCP HTTP
        participant HTTPD as httpd CGI<br/>8080/TCP HTTP
        participant CGI as access.cgi<br/>(bash script)
        participant CS as code-server<br/>8888/TCP HTTP

        Controller->>KRBP: Poll /api/kernels/<br/>HTTPS / Bearer Token
        KRBP->>Nginx: Forward request<br/>HTTP (pod-internal)
        Nginx->>HTTPD: Proxy to CGI gateway<br/>HTTP (pod-internal)
        HTTPD->>CGI: Execute CGI script
        CGI->>CS: Check code-server healthz<br/>HTTP (localhost)
        CS-->>CGI: Heartbeat response
        CGI-->>HTTPD: JSON activity status
        HTTPD-->>Nginx: CGI response
        Nginx-->>KRBP: Activity status
        KRBP-->>Controller: /api/kernels/ response
    end
